        "summary":  "Anthropic released Claude Opus 5 on July 24, 2026, delivering improved performance on coding and knowledge tasks at identical pricing to its predecessor ($5 per million input tokens, $25 per million output tokens). The model exceeded all competing models on Frontier-Bench v0.1 benchmarks and achieved within 0.5% of Fable 5\u0027s peak score on CursorBench 3.2 at half the cost per task. Beta features include mid-conversation tool changes and automatic fallbacks, available on the Claude Platform and API.",
        "execSummary":  "Claude Opus 5\u0027s same-price, higher-performance release is a direct competitive move against OpenAI and Google ΓÇö enterprises currently benchmarking frontier models for agentic coding or knowledge-intensive tasks should rerun evaluations with Opus 5 before finalizing platform commitments. The CursorBench result at half the cost per task is the headline number for enterprise buyers: if it holds in production, it represents a material ROI improvement for organizations running Opus-class workloads. The beta automatic fallback feature is particularly relevant for production deployments, as it addresses reliability risk in multi-step agent pipelines where a single tool call failure can break an entire workflow. Monitor the Fable 5 benchmark gap closely ΓÇö Anthropic is framing it as near-parity, but that 0.5% spread on a single benchmark warrants broader evaluation before treating the models as interchangeable.",
        "vendorLean":  "Anthropic",
