        "execSummary":  "The decision that matters here is vendor diversification at the infrastructure layer: Microsoft is no longer betting exclusively on NVIDIA for AI compute, giving enterprise customers more flexibility and leverage in procurement. For organizations planning large-scale AI inference or technical computing workloads, these AMD-powered VM families offer an alternative pricing and performance tier worth evaluating. The broader implication is that the hyperscaler AI infrastructure race is accelerating, which generally keeps prices competitive and accelerates capability availability. Watch for whether AMD\u0027s Helios platform delivers on inference benchmarks against NVIDIA H100/H200 equivalents before committing to long-term contracts.",
