        "summary":  "Google CEO Sundar Pichai used I/O 2026 to declare the arrival of the \u0027agentic Gemini era,\u0027 announcing Gemini Omni Flash (multimodal video generation), Gemini 3.5 Flash (frontier-speed at lower cost), and Gemini Spark (a 24/7 personal AI agent). Google reported processing over 3.2 quadrillion tokens per month, representing 7x year-over-year growth. New 8th-generation TPUs enable distributed training across one million units globally.",
        "execSummary":  "Google\u0027s I/O 2026 keynote signals a decisive shift from AI as a feature to AI as an ambient operating layer across search, workspace, and personal productivity ΓÇö a strategic posture every enterprise AI roadmap should benchmark against. The 7x token growth figure is the most important data point: it confirms that enterprise AI consumption is scaling faster than most organizations\u0027 internal adoption plans. For customer-support leaders, Gemini Spark\u0027s 24/7 long-horizon agent capabilities preview the next generation of autonomous support tooling beyond today\u0027s copilots. The caveat is that Google\u0027s consumer-first framing means enterprise governance, compliance, and data-residency requirements will lag behind the capability announcements.",
