        "source":  "Google AI Blog",
        "url":  "https://blog.google/innovation-and-ai/technology/developers-tools/interactions-api-general-availability/",
        "date":  "2026-07-01",
        "theme":  "Platforms",
        "summary":  "Google announced the general availability of the Interactions API, a unified endpoint for both Gemini model inference and autonomous agent execution with server-side state, background execution, and multimodal generation. After launching in public beta in December 2025, the stable API now supports Managed Agents, long-running background tasks, built-in Google Search and Maps tools combined with custom functions, and Deep Research enhancements. It is now the default interface across Google AI Studio and official documentation.",
        "execSummary":  "General availability of the Interactions API is a platform consolidation move that matters strategically: Google is collapsing the distinction between calling a model and running an agent into a single, stateful endpoint, which significantly lowers the engineering barrier for enterprises building multi-step AI workflows. For customer-support platform architects, the combination of built-in Search, Maps, and custom function tools in one API call means complex, tool-augmented support agents can now be built with far less glue code. The stable schema commitment gives enterprises the greenlight to move beyond pilots into production integrations. The caveat: the legacy generateContent API remains supported, so migration is not urgent, but teams that defer will accumulate technical debt as new capabilities concentrate in the Interactions API.",
