        "url":  "https://www.technologyreview.com/2026/07/27/1140668/building-the-enterprise-environment-for-agentic-ai/",
        "date":  "2026-07-27",
        "theme":  "Agents",
        "summary":  "This Intel-sponsored article examines the systems-level challenges of deploying agentic AI in enterprise environments, arguing that inference speed alone is insufficient and that success requires holistic infrastructure covering data access, tool execution, and scalability. Intel\u0027s research identified five key lessons, including measuring performance through agent density and task latency rather than traditional CPU utilization metrics. Scale-out architectures are recommended as the default for most enterprise agent deployments.",
        "execSummary":  "The article reframes agentic AI as a systems integration challenge rather than a model performance challenge, which is the right lens for enterprise leaders evaluating infrastructure readiness for AI agent deployments at scale. Measuring agent density and task latency rather than conventional CPU metrics is a practical shift that will require new operational tooling and SLA definitions for any team running production AI agents. For customer-support operations, this means existing infrastructure benchmarks likely undercount what is actually needed to run reliable, low-latency AI agents at volume. The key caveat is that this is sponsored content from Intel, so the infrastructure recommendations are naturally biased toward compute-intensive, scale-out solutions over alternative architectures.",
