        "date":  "2026-07-27",
        "theme":  "Orchestration",
        "summary":  "Outshift by Cisco proposes an \u0027Internet of Cognition\u0027 framework for achieving artificial superintelligence through horizontal scaling of multi-agent systems rather than scaling individual models. The framework includes a semantic coordination layer that enables autonomous AI agents to share intent, context, and reasoning across domains. Open-source tools AGNTCY and Mycelium are presented as infrastructure for agents to discover each other, align goals, and collaborate on complex problems without human intervention.",
        "execSummary":  "The \u0027Internet of Cognition\u0027 concept represents a significant architectural bet ΓÇö that superintelligence emerges from coordinated agent networks, not from ever-larger single models ΓÇö and Cisco is positioning its networking expertise as the infrastructure backbone for that future. For enterprise AI strategists, this is a preview of where multi-agent orchestration is heading: from human-supervised pipelines to autonomous agent meshes that negotiate and self-organize around complex tasks. The near-term implication is that enterprise orchestration standards (how agents discover, trust, and hand off to each other) will matter as much as the models themselves, and early standardization choices will create long-term architectural lock-in. The caveat is that this is sponsored Cisco content, framing their networking assets as essential infrastructure for a multi-agent future that remains largely theoretical.",
